                                                "sense_id": "6ecd6e73-ed2a-3b8a-8405-51ad3ad782eb",
                                                "text": "Mondriaan war ein Vertreter des Konstruktivismus."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb4619b5-8625-3b99-a4a2-963a0c0152ea",
                                        "entry_id": "f7aadaf3-c4c0-3658-a117-16e32f4f36bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Richtung innerhalb der russischen Literatur, deren Vertreter sich um die Bedingungen der proletarischen Kunst bemühten"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fddc77cf-4dfc-486b-8ef5-dbc8b6cccb12",
                                                "sense_id": "eb4619b5-8625-3b99-a4a2-963a0c0152ea",
                                                "text": "Juri liest vorzugsweise Bücher des Konstruktivismus."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf240f4f-2620-3deb-a3f5-bb3a6e8ddce6",
                                        "entry_id": "f7aadaf3-c4c0-3658-a117-16e32f4f36bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Denkweise, die von der Konstruktion der Realität durch den Betrachter ausgeht"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Erkenntnistheorie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "615eeafd-d2c2-439b-9ba4-b2e2c7ce37ef",
                                                "sense_id": "cf240f4f-2620-3deb-a3f5-bb3a6e8ddce6",
                                                "text": "Der Konstruktivismus hat eine andere Auffassung von der Realität als der Realismus."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60cbd46c-5f41-35b5-9ba9-5ed8ba31946c",
                                        "entry_id": "f7aadaf3-c4c0-3658-a117-16e32f4f36bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Stilrichtung der (vor allem sowjetischen) Baukunst"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b13a7ec0-5067-4e63-92b3-f89a8def535d",
                                                "sense_id": "60cbd46c-5f41-35b5-9ba9-5ed8ba31946c",
                                                "text": "„Allein in Moskau gibt es noch rund 70 Gebäude im damals entwickelten Stil, dem Konstruktivismus, darunter Fabriken und Kommunenhäuser.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"4\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3785cfa3-f93c-36df-9099-aeb5b89518e7",
                                        "entry_id": "f7aadaf3-c4c0-3658-a117-16e32f4f36bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "einer von mehreren umfassenden metatheoretischen Ansätzen auf dem Gebiet der Internationalen Beziehungen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Internationale Beziehungen"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "246023ff-b159-4d02-ab3f-274641e57450",
                                                "sense_id": "3785cfa3-f93c-36df-9099-aeb5b89518e7",
                                                "text": "„Der politikwissenschaftliche Konstruktivismus zielt auf die Erklärung von politischen Handlungsmustern. Typisch ist dabei, dass in Anlehnung an Grundideen sonstiger konstruktivistischer Theorien in der Philosophie und in Nachbarwissenschaften Handlung als Ergebnis einer sozialen Situation bzw. von vorherrschenden sozialen Strukturen verstanden wird.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"5\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bfa50551-905a-4624-a5e6-b3e9ea01c09f",
                        "source_entry_id": "eca10c6c-47b6-3490-bf3f-767f0d043f7f",
                        "target_lang_word": "constructivism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "constructivism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d295673e-c52c-3e0f-9d76-4affecd176fb",
                                        "entry_id": "8f33f425-45a4-3bcb-ba25-01f5cbdd3431",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Russian movement in modern art characterized by the creation of nonrepresentational geometric objects using industrial materials."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4989ba09-cd26-3c54-bb6f-e81ba9d34f75",
                                        "entry_id": "8f33f425-45a4-3bcb-ba25-01f5cbdd3431",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A philosophy that asserts the need to construct a mathematical object to prove it exists."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a989acd-97be-3ce2-9754-8a36869a5358",
                                        "entry_id": "8f33f425-45a4-3bcb-ba25-01f5cbdd3431",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A psychological epistemology which argues that humans generate knowledge and meaning from their experiences."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ee38e6b-8881-48eb-9518-4cacd726a6c0",
                                                "sense_id": "4a989acd-97be-3ce2-9754-8a36869a5358",
                                                "text": "There is no single theory of constructivism. In fact, there are many shades and varieties of constructivism spanning a range of perspectives. There is also no single individual who can be identified as the founder of constructivism. In fact, rather than tracing a linear development along one line of philosophical thought, constructivism seems to circumscribe a set of thinkers, theories and approaches that spring from a plethora of historical and cultural origins."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e06903c-a914-4e93-a362-b067f59f2567",
                                                "sense_id": "4a989acd-97be-3ce2-9754-8a36869a5358",
                                                "text": "According to constructivism, all systems are artificial abstractions. They are not made by nature and presented to use to be discovered, but we construct them by our perceptual and mental capabilities with the domain of our experiences."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
